==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|bawlen|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|non|en}} {{term|baula||to low|lang=non}} and/or {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|baulō||bark|pos=verb|lang=la}}, both from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*bau-||to roar}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*bau-||to bark}}, conflated with {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*bellaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ballijaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*buljaną||to shout, low, roar}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*bʰel-||to sound, roar}}. Cognate with {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|baula||to moo, low|lang=is}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|böla||to bellow, low|lang=sv}}. More at {{l/en|bell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|[bɔːɫ]}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/bɔl/}}
* {{a|cot-caught}} {{IPA|/bɑl/}}
* {{rhymes|ɔːl}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|ball}}<!--perhaps not in all dialects but in Australian English and in New York City-->

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[shout]] or [[utter]] in a loud and [[intense]] manner.
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[wail]]; to give out a [[blaring]] [[cry]].

